    "# Phase 4 — Signal Preprocessing\n",
    "## Step 2 & 3: Preprocessing Foundation, DC Offset Removal, & Windowing Strategy\n",
    "\n",
    "### Objective\n",
    "The goal of this notebook is to establish a reproducible preprocessing and windowing pipeline for the NASA IMS Bearing Dataset (Set 2) while preserving raw data immutability and degradation trends.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Preprocessing & Windowing Strategy Principles:\n",
    "1. **Optional Mean Centering:** $x_{\\text{centered}} = x - \\mu_{\\text{snapshot}}$ subtracts static sensor bias without altering standard deviation or peak-to-peak amplitude.\n",
    "2. **Preservation of Degradation Growth:** No per-snapshot z-scoring is applied, preserving original RMS and variance growth over time.\n",
    "3. **Modular Windowing:** Snapshots ($20,480$ samples) can be segmented into sub-windows ($N_{\\text{window}} = 2048$ or $20,480$) with configurable overlap ratios."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Cell 1: Environment Setup & Helper Imports\n",
    "import sys\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "\n",
    "# Ensure project root is in sys.path\n",
    "project_root = Path.cwd().parent if Path.cwd().name == \"notebooks\" else Path.cwd()\n",
    "if str(project_root) not in sys.path:\n",
    "    sys.path.insert(0, str(project_root))\n",
    "\n",
    "from src.data_loading import get_snapshot_files, parse_snapshot_timestamp, load_snapshot\n",
    "from src.preprocessing import remove_dc_offset, process_snapshot, extract_windows, DEFAULT_MANIFEST_PATH\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Preprocessing notebook setup complete.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Cell 2 Explanation: Loading Dataset Manifest\n",
    "We load the generated dataset manifest (`data/processed/manifest_set2.csv`) to verify file validity and snapshot indices."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Cell 2: Inspect Dataset Manifest Summary\n",
    "manifest_df = pd.read_csv(DEFAULT_MANIFEST_PATH)\n",
    "print(f\"Total manifest records: {len(manifest_df)}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Valid snapshots count: {(manifest_df['is_valid'] == True).sum()}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nManifest Notes Breakdown:\")\n",
    "display(manifest_df[\"notes\"].value_counts().to_frame())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--- \n",
    "## Comparing Raw vs. Centered Representations\n",
    "\n",
    "We evaluate 3 representative snapshots:\n",
    "1. **Early Baseline Snapshot (File 0):** `2004.02.12.10.32.39`\n",
    "2. **High-Amplitude Snapshot (File 979, Index -5):** `2004.02.19.05.42.39`\n",
    "3. **Final Low-Amplitude Snapshot (File 983, Index -1):** `2004.02.19.06.22.39`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Cell 3: Define 3 Representative Snapshots\n",
    "files = get_snapshot_files()\n",
    "\n",
    "target_snapshots = [\n",
    "    (\"Early Baseline (File 0)\", files[0]),\n",
    "    (\"High-Amplitude (File 979)\", files[-5]),\n",
    "    (\"Final Low-Amplitude (File 983)\", files[-1])\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Target Snapshots Selected for Comparison:\")\n",
    "for label, f in target_snapshots:\n",
    "    print(f\" - {label}: {f.name} ({parse_snapshot_timestamp(f)})\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Cell 4 Explanation: Quantitative Statistical Comparison\n",
    "We calculate and compare 4 statistical metrics between **Raw** and **Centered** signals:\n",
    "- **Mean:** Shifted to $0.0$ after mean centering.\n",
    "- **Standard Deviation (Std):** $100\\%$ identical.\n",
    "- **Peak-to-Peak (P2P = Max - Min):** $100\\%$ identical.\n",
    "- **RMS:** Slightly shifted from $\\sqrt{\\text{mean}^2 + \\text{std}^2}$ to $\\text{std}$."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Cell 4: Compute & Display Side-by-Side Statistical Comparison\n",
    "comparison_rows = []\n",
    "\n",
    "for stage_name, file_path in target_snapshots:\n",
    "    df_raw = load_snapshot(file_path)\n",
    "    df_cent = remove_dc_offset(df_raw)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    for ch in df_raw.columns:\n",
    "        raw_mean = df_raw[ch].mean()\n",
    "        cent_mean = df_cent[ch].mean()\n",
    "        \n",
    "        raw_std = df_raw[ch].std()\n",
    "        cent_std = df_cent[ch].std()\n",
    "        \n",
    "        raw_rms = np.sqrt((df_raw[ch]**2).mean())\n",
    "        cent_rms = np.sqrt((df_cent[ch]**2).mean())\n",
    "        \n",
    "        raw_p2p = df_raw[ch].max() - df_raw[ch].min()\n",
    "        cent_p2p = df_cent[ch].max() - df_cent[ch].min()\n",
    "        \n",
    "        comparison_rows.append({\n",
    "            \"Stage\": stage_name,\n",
    "            \"Channel\": ch,\n",
    "            \"Raw Mean\": raw_mean,\n",
    "            \"Cent Mean\": cent_mean,\n",
    "            \"Raw Std\": raw_std,\n",
    "            \"Cent Std\": cent_std,\n",
    "            \"Raw RMS\": raw_rms,\n",
    "            \"Cent RMS\": cent_rms,\n",
    "            \"Raw P2P\": raw_p2p,\n",
    "            \"Cent P2P\": cent_p2p\n",
    "        })\n",
    "\n",
    "df_comparison = pd.DataFrame(comparison_rows)\n",
    "print(\"Side-by-Side Statistical Comparison (Raw vs. Centered):\")\n",
    "display(df_comparison)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Cell 5 Explanation: Visualizing Raw vs. Centered Signals\n",
    "We plot raw vs. centered waveforms for Channel 1 across the 3 representative snapshots to visually demonstrate that mean subtraction shifts the baseline to 0.0 without changing signal shape or dynamic range."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Cell 5: Plot Raw vs. Centered Waveforms (Channel 1)\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(3, 1, figsize=(13, 8), sharex=True)\n",
    "fig.suptitle(\"Channel 1 Signal Comparison: Raw vs. Centered (Mean-Subtracted)\", fontsize=13, fontweight=\"bold\")\n",
    "\n",
    "for i, (stage_name, file_path) in enumerate(target_snapshots):\n",
    "    ax = axes[i]\n",
    "    df_raw = load_snapshot(file_path)\n",
    "    df_cent = remove_dc_offset(df_raw)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Plot zoomed segment (first 1000 samples) for visual clarity\n",
    "    ax.plot(df_raw[\"Channel_1\"].iloc[:1000], label=\"Raw Signal\", color=\"#1f77b4\", alpha=0.7, linewidth=1)\n",
    "    ax.plot(df_cent[\"Channel_1\"].iloc[:1000], label=\"Centered Signal\", color=\"#d62728\", linestyle=\"--\", alpha=0.9, linewidth=1)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    ax.set_title(f\"{stage_name} — {file_path.name}\", fontsize=10)\n",
    "    ax.set_ylabel(\"Amplitude\", fontsize=9)\n",
    "    ax.grid(True, linestyle=\"--\", alpha=0.5)\n",
    "    if i == 0:\n",
    "        ax.legend(loc=\"upper right\", fontsize=9)\n",
    "\n",
    "axes[-1].set_xlabel(\"Sample Index (Zoomed First 1,000 Points)\", fontsize=10)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--- \n",
    "## Step 3: Windowing Strategy & Implementation\n",
    "\n",
    "### Beginner-Friendly Concepts\n",
    "1. **What Windowing Is:**\n",
    "   Windowing partitions a $20,480$-sample snapshot ($1\\text{ second}$) into smaller sub-segments ($N_{\\text{window}}$) to calculate localized statistical features or spectral properties over time.\n",
    "2. **Window Length Trade-offs ($N_{\\text{window}}$):**\n",
    "   - **1,024 samples ($\approx 50\\text{ ms}$):** High time resolution (20 windows per snapshot), but higher computational overhead and higher statistical variance per window.\n",
    "   - **2,048 samples ($\approx 100\\text{ ms}$):** Balanced configuration (10 non-overlapping windows per snapshot). Good balance of statistical stability and frequency resolution ($\\Delta f = 10\\text{ Hz}$).\n",
    "   - **4,096 samples ($\approx 200\\text{ ms}$):** Lower time resolution (5 windows per snapshot). Excellent statistical stability.\n",
    "   - **20,480 samples ($1,000\\text{ ms}$ / full snapshot):** Baseline configuration (1 window per snapshot $\\rightarrow 984$ total feature vectors). Zero segmentation overhead.\n",
    "3. **Overlapping vs. Non-Overlapping Windows:**\n",
    "   - **Non-overlapping ($0\\%$ overlap):** Simple, zero data redundancy, 10 windows per snapshot ($N=2048$).\n",
    "   - **Overlapping ($50\\%$ overlap):** Adjacent windows overlap by $50\\%$ (step size $S=1024$). Smooths window-to-window feature transitions, yielding 19 windows per snapshot."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Cell 6: Demonstrate Window Slicing on the First Snapshot (File 0)\n",
    "df_snapshot = load_snapshot(files[0])\n",
    "\n",
    "# 1. Extract non-overlapping windows (N=2048, 0% overlap)\n",
    "wins_non_overlap = extract_windows(df_snapshot, window_length=2048, overlap_ratio=0.0)\n",
    "\n",
    "# 2. Extract overlapping windows (N=2048, 50% overlap)\n",
    "wins_50_overlap = extract_windows(df_snapshot, window_length=2048, overlap_ratio=0.5)\n",
    "\n",
    "# 3. Extract baseline full snapshot window (N=20480, 0% overlap)\n",
    "wins_full_snapshot = extract_windows(df_snapshot, window_length=20480, overlap_ratio=0.0)\n",
    "\n",
    "windowing_summary = pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "    \"Windowing Configuration\": [\n",
    "        \"Full Snapshot (N=20480, 0% overlap)\",\n",
    "        \"Sub-window Non-overlapping (N=2048, 0% overlap)\",\n",
    "        \"Sub-window 50% Overlap (N=2048, 50% overlap)\"\n",
    "    ],\n",
    "    \"Windows per Snapshot\": [\n",
    "        len(wins_full_snapshot),\n",
    "        len(wins_non_overlap),\n",
    "        len(wins_50_overlap)\n",
    "    ],\n",
    "    \"Total Dataset Windows (984 Files)\": [\n",
    "        len(wins_full_snapshot) * len(files),\n",
    "        len(wins_non_overlap) * len(files),\n",
    "        len(wins_50_overlap) * len(files)\n",
    "    ],\n",
    "    \"Window Shape\": [\n",
    "        str(wins_full_snapshot[0].shape),\n",
    "        str(wins_non_overlap[0].shape),\n",
    "        str(wins_50_overlap[0].shape)\n",
    "    ]\n",
    "})\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Windowing Configurations Slicing Summary:\")\n",
    "display(windowing_summary)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Cell 7 Explanation: Intra-Snapshot Sub-Window Statistics\n",
    "We compute RMS and Standard Deviation across the 10 sub-windows of the early baseline snapshot to observe sub-second statistical stability."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Cell 7: Compute Statistics Across Sub-Windows of Snapshot 0 (Channel 1)\n",
    "sub_window_stats = []\n",
    "for w_idx, win in enumerate(wins_non_overlap):\n",
    "    sub_window_stats.append({\n",
    "        \"Sub-Window Index\": w_idx,\n",
    "        \"Start Sample\": w_idx * 2048,\n",
    "        \"End Sample\": (w_idx + 1) * 2048 - 1,\n",
    "        \"Channel_1 Mean\": win[\"Channel_1\"].mean(),\n",
    "        \"Channel_1 Std\": win[\"Channel_1\"].std(),\n",
    "        \"Channel_1 RMS\": np.sqrt((win[\"Channel_1\"]**2).mean()),\n",
    "        \"Channel_1 P2P\": win[\"Channel_1\"].max() - win[\"Channel_1\"].min()\n",
    "    })\n",
    "\n",
    "df_sub_stats = pd.DataFrame(sub_window_stats)\n",
    "print(\"Sub-Window Statistical Metrics (Snapshot 0, Channel 1, N=2048):\")\n",
    "display(df_sub_stats)"
   ]
  }
